  "body": "## What changed\n\nMain is red on `plunge_depth_tab::the_tabbed_contour_catalog_case_names_its_tab_window_dives`. Two PRs crossed:\n\n- PR #3866 (#3678) made each tab window dive of the `2d/contour-tabs` catalog case peck one stepdown at a time.\n- PR #3847 (#3679) merged after it. Its test pinned the three dives that the verifier named before the peck.\n\nThe test header said that the test changes on purpose when #3678 lands. It now pins:\n\n- The verifier names no `PlungeTooDeep` finding for the case.\n- The path pecks: tab windows 1 to 3 each dive Z4, Z2, Z0 from the Z6 stock top. No feed goes more than the 2 mm stepdown below the depth before it.\n\nThe second check reads the path, so the test also fails if the verifier stops seeing the dives. The decision is in `docs/decisions/3920-plunge-depth-tab-after-peck.md`.\n\n## How tested\n\n- Before the change, I generated the case and read the path: the three dives peck Z4, Z2, Z0, and the toolpath has no warnings.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test plunge_depth_tab` passes. Clippy with `-D warnings` is clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick`: 1 of 1 step passes.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNo generator or verifier code changed.\n\nChangelog: none (test only).\nEffort: low\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nFixes #3920\n",
